// Date: 2020-07-30 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1055.001
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects specific process characteristics of Chinese TAIDOOR RAT malware load
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://us-cert.cisa.gov/ncas/analysis-reports/ar20-216a
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2020/TA/TAIDOOR-RAT/proc_creation_win_apt_taidoor.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "dll,MyStart" or ProcessCommandLine contains "dll MyStart") or (ProcessCommandLine endswith " MyStart" and ProcessCommandLine contains "rundll32.exe")
